  "brief_rationale": "The model repeatedly checked current red flags, explicitly prioritized the high-risk ACS/heart-failure episode, and set safe medication boundaries (no self-stopping of clopidogrel, distinguishing inpatient IV orders from home oral drugs, and directing verification with the cardiology team). It never fabricated results or urged discharge. All eight responsibility-chain items are met with at most a few minor gaps in RC5/RC8 that do not rise to serious error. However, no high-order point was fully completed with meaningful trajectory impact—HO1, HO2, HO3, and HO4 were all triggered but only partially addressed, and the trajectory reached valid_open closure with an executable, traceable plan and family receipt. Because no serious or minor in-chain error exists, but also no completed high-order point, the grade is capped at 3 (Acceptable).",
